{# ONE GROUPED DROPDOWN OF THE HOUSE FILTER BAR.

   A CLOSED CHIP THAT OPENS A PANEL OF OPTIONS WITH LIVE COUNTS — the
   incidents pattern, which is the standing rule for every filter bar in the
   product.

   IT IS A `<details>`, AND EVERY OPTION IS A LINK. The address is the state,
   so a filtered list is a link somebody can send and a page a browser can go
   back to; and the whole control opens, chooses and clears with no script of
   ours, which is what keeps a filter bar working on a page that has none.

   AN OPTION IS A VALUE, A LABEL, A COUNT AND SOMETIMES A COLOUR. A role
   filters by the word it is spelt with; a zone filters by an identifier and
   reads as a name with its own hue. One control serves both because the
   caller hands it {@see Uhifadhi\Bundle\AreaBundle\Model\FilterOption}s
   rather than a map it would have to guess the shape of.

   THE COUNTS ARE OF THE WHOLE SET, not of what is already filtered: a count
   that moved as you filtered could not tell you what picking an option would
   do, which is the one thing it is for. #}
{% set picked = chosenLabel is defined and chosenLabel is not null ? chosenLabel : chosen %}
<details class="i-dd">
    <summary class="mchip i-ddt{{ chosen is not null ? ' on' : '' }}">
        <span class="i-ddval">{{ picked is not null ? picked : all|raw }}</span>
        <span class="i-ddcaret">&#9662;</span>
    </summary>
    <div class="i-ddmenu">
        <span class="i-ddhead">{{ label|raw }}</span>
        <a class="i-ddopt{{ chosen ? '' : ' on' }}"
           href="{{ path(app.request.attributes.get('_route'), app.request.attributes.get('_route_params')|merge(query.with(key, null))) }}">
            <span class="i-ddopt-l">{{ all|raw }}</span>
        </a>
        <span class="i-ddsep"></span>
        {% for option in options %}
            <a class="i-ddopt{{ chosen == option.value ? ' on' : '' }}"
               href="{{ path(app.request.attributes.get('_route'), app.request.attributes.get('_route_params')|merge(query.with(key, option.value))) }}">
                {% if option.hue %}<span class="i-dot" style="background:{{ option.hue }}"></span>{% endif %}
                <span class="i-ddopt-l">{{ option.label }}</span>
                {% if option.count > 0 %}<span class="i-ddopt-n">{{ option.count }}</span>{% endif %}
            </a>
        {% endfor %}
    </div>
</details>
